      "text_raw": "In weak inversion, the trans-\nconductance is proportional\nto the current. Maintaining\na constant current over\nthe whole common-mode\ninput range will provide\na constant total trans-\nconductance.\nThere is one problem\nhowever. The factor n is\ndifferent for nMOST and\npMOST devices. Remember\nthat this n factor is not very\nprecise because it contains\nthe depletion layer capaci-\ntance, which depends on\nbiasing voltages.\nNevertheless, it is vital to try to compensate for this difference in the n factor. An error in\ntransconductance will otherwise result.",
      "text": "In weak inversion, the transconductance is proportional to the current. Maintaining a constant current over the whole common-mode input range will provide a constant total transconductance. There is one problem however. The factor n is different for nMOST and pMOST devices. Remember that this n factor is not very precise because it contains the depletion layer capacitance, which depends on biasing voltages. Nevertheless, it is vital to try to compensate for this difference in the n factor. An error in transconductance will otherwise result."
    }
